    core: `The Sun, conscious identity and the drive toward purposeful self-definition, and Mercury, the mind, perception, and the function of articulation that converts thought into form, are separated by 120 degrees, placing them in the same elemental family. The trine means these two forces do not experience each other as foreign. The conscious self and the thinking self are oriented toward compatible ends, drawing on the same elemental register, supporting each other without effort. This person's voice tends to sound like them. What they think and what they identify with run on the same current.`,
    behavioral: `The trine between the Sun's identity-function and Mercury's cognitive function creates a well-integrated articulating self. The mind serves the conscious will rather than running on a separate track, and the conscious will is articulate about its own ends rather than driving forward without intellectual self-awareness. This person can describe what they want, why they want it, and how they propose to pursue it without significant internal friction in any of those operations. The cognitive style tends to be clear without being cold, verbal without being verbose, and articulate without performing articulacy. The shadow of this trine is the same shadow it carries everywhere: ease can produce comfortable underdevelopment of either function, since neither identity nor mind is forced into the kind of contention that produces depth.`,
